-- A rule whose reason runs over two lines, written with a line break inside
-- the string. See boolean-rules.l4 for what an "agreement:" line says, and
-- for `pad`.
--
-- agreement: `the fee` may refuse with ["this schedule is not encoded:\nyears before 2000 follow the old schedule"]
-- agreement: `the fee` {"year": 2001} => answers 100
-- agreement: `the fee` {"year": 1999} => refuses "this schedule is not encoded:\nyears before 2000 follow the old schedule"

@export the fee for a year
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee` year pad MEANS
  IF year AT LEAST 2000 THEN 100
  ELSE REFUSE "this schedule is not encoded:
years before 2000 follow the old schedule"
